"""GPU ground truth for the FP4, ``.rs``, ``ue8m0``, and ``.scaled`` PTX ``cvt`` forms.

Captured from real hardware, not from a reference implementation:

* device   NVIDIA B200 (compute capability 10.0)
* driver   595.58.03
* toolkit  CUDA 13.2, V13.2.51 (PTX ISA 9.2)
* build    ``nvcc -gencode=arch=compute_100a,code=sm_100a``
* run      ``CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=1``

Companion to `ptx_cvt_fp8_goldens`, which covers the packed FP8 family.  Each
kernel is a single inline-PTX ``cvt`` with the exact spelling the TIRx frontend
emits for the matching form — including the ``.b8`` staging the frontend wraps
around every ``e2m1x2`` operand and result — so the goldens pin the instruction
as a kernel can actually reach it.  ``-gencode`` is spelled out because plain
``-arch=sm_100a`` compiles the device PTX at ``.target sm_100``, where *every*
spelling below is rejected.

Coverage of the eight input sections:

* ``F32_SOURCE`` — signed zeros, binary32 subnormals including the ``2**-127``
  boundary the ``ue8m0`` roundings turn on and the largest subnormal (just under
  ``2**-126``, where a ``log2``-based exponent encoder disagrees with hardware);
  the whole e2m1 grid with every tie and the values just off each tie; e4m3 and
  e5m2 boundaries; exact powers of two with the value one ulp below; ``.rs``
  residues at ``m/256`` of an e4m3, e5m2 and e2m1 ulp; non-finite values of both
  signs, quiet and signalling.
* ``F16X2_SOURCE`` / ``BF16X2_SOURCE`` — the same special values in the packed
  16-bit formats, paired so each appears in both halves.
* ``F4X2_SOURCE`` — ``range(256)``, so the ``e2m1x2`` unpack forms are covered
  exhaustively.
* ``F8X2_SOURCE`` / ``UE8X2_SOURCE`` — ``(byte << 8) | (255 - byte)`` for every
  byte, so all 256 encodings appear in both the upper and the lower half.
* ``SCALE_SOURCE`` — every ordered pair of sixteen interesting ``ue8m0`` scale
  bytes, from total underflow through unity to the NaN encoding ``255``.
* ``RBITS_SOURCE`` — zero, all ones, every single bit, every single byte, and
  structured plus pseudo-random words.

The two-primary forms convert ``(a, b) = (source[i], source[(i + 1) % n])`` and
the ``.rs`` forms ``(a, b, e, f) = source[i .. i + 3]``, which places every
source value in every operand position.

Regenerated by ``tests/numsim/microtests/cases/ptx_cvt_narrow_goldens.cu``.
"""

from __future__ import annotations

import numpy as np


def _u16(text: str) -> np.ndarray:
    return np.frombuffer(bytes.fromhex(text), dtype=">u2").astype(np.uint16)


def _u32(text: str) -> np.ndarray:
    return np.frombuffer(bytes.fromhex(text), dtype=">u4").astype(np.uint32)


